0,Trinidadian Creole - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinidadian_Creole,Trinidadian Creole is an English-based creole language commonly spoken throughout the island of Trinidad in Trinidad and Tobago. It is distinct from Tobagonian Creole – particularly at the basilectal level – and from other Lesser Antillean creoles.,Trinidadian English Creole,Creole
